WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.134
-Our first guest tonight served

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.303
as United States senator
from Massachusetts,

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.038
and secretary of state
for President Obama.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:08.241
He is now the special
presidential envoy for climate,

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.543
as part of the United States
National Security Council.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.912
Please welcome back
to the show John Kerry.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:17.050
[ Applause ]
♪♪

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.818
-Hi, Seth.
-Thank you for being back.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.786
-Good to see you, man.
-Good to see you, too.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:21.854
Thank you.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:26.026
♪♪

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.860
-Welcome. It is lovely
to have you here.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.332
I know we have you here in town
because of the UN.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.967
Do you feel like
you're making progress?

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.301
-Yeah, I do.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.338
Can I begin just by saying
thank you for doing this,

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.939
for joining with your fellow
late night hosts?

00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:43.676
It's fantastic and you do
an incredible Bernie Sanders.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.211
-Thank you.
-It's great.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.946
-That means the most to me
and I only wish

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.382
my Bernie could stop
the warming of our planet.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.250
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.252
-I think he's warming
the planet, actually.

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:57.090
-Yeah, maybe just get him
to quiet down a little.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.692
I want to ask real quick
because the UN had maybe --

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.161
and, again, you're a big star,
special envoy --

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.462
but, on Monday...
-I don't know.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:07.600
-...BTS performed.
-I know. I know. They're great.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.735
-John Kerry's a BTS fan?

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.669
-I watched the video there.

00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:11.738
You know, what is it,

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.339
"Permission to Dance"
or something?

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.140
It's fantastic.
-Yeah. They know what
they're doing, right?

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.443
-Well, you know you see them.
I travel a lot, nowadays,

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.645
and you see them
in all these advertisements.

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.480
You know, when they're
prepping the airplane,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.516
they're doing one thing.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.018
-It's kind of crazy.
Want to get up and --

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.153
-[ Laughs ]
-No.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.855
-I would love you not to.
-But they're fun.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.759
A lot of people I know
would love me not to.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.760
No, but they're really good.
They are good.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.763
-And they're taking this
seriously as well

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.164
and I think a lot
of young people, right now,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.733
are sort of getting wise
to the fact that

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.301
this is going to be
their planet for a lot longer

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:44.270
than it's going to be your
and my planet.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.806
Is there any reason for them
to be optimistic right now?

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:50.043
-Yes. I mean, there is a reason
to be optimistic.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.711
There's also a reason
to be hopeful.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.446
Very hopeful.

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:55.848
You know, just yesterday,

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:59.252
President Biden upped the ante
of what the United States

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.220
is going to do
to support the transition

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.790
and to help convert
to electric cars

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.459
and all the things
we need to do.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.696
And he's committed
about $11 billion

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.332
that the United States
is going to deploy,

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.233
in order to help the transition.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:15.334
But, equally importantly,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.536
he's got major legislation
in the Congress.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:20.540
Try to deploy 500,000

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.508
electric vehicle
charging stations

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.611
to accelerate this transition.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:28.915
A tax credit for production,
for investment.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.484
We have to invest.
I mean, in order to get there,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.753
Seth, we have to invest

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.722
trillions of dollars
over the next 30 years.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.790
No government
has the kind of money

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.458
that's going to make
this transition happen,

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:43.062
so what really encourages me
is the private sector.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.564
They are stepping up

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:47.133
and you have CEOs all
around the world,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.435
you have major
financial institutions,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.570
that are prepared to invest

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.440
literally trillions of dollars
in the next 10 years,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.643
which, the scientists tell us,
is the critical period.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:03:00.179
-It does seem like
there are some moderates,

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.513
even on the Democratic side,

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:04.150
who are maybe trying
to slow this down a little bit.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:08.988
Has it been frustrating for you
that it doesn't seem to be

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.423
that the entire party
is taking this

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.024
as seriously as they should?

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.125
-No, I think they're
taking it seriously.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:15.294
What frustrates me
are the people who think

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:17.363
that ivermectin
is going to solve the problem.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.966
-No, yeah, they're problematic.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.267
-You know, I mean,

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.836
there's so much disinformation.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.238
There's a whole party that's
waiting for the MyPillow guy

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:27.439
to give them a clue as to what

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:29.208
they ought to do, right?
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.409
-That's a problem.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:31.611
I mean, seriously.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.313
We've lost years, here.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.381
We lost three years
with President Trump.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.083
He pulled
out of the Paris Agreement.

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.553
Thank God that governors,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.988
Republicans and Democrats,
alike,

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:45.457
continue to deploy their

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.327
renewable portfolio laws
in the states.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:51.531
So America isn't as far behind
as some people think,

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.198
but the world is far behind.

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:56.903
All of us together really have,

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:59.305
you know, a shortened amount
of time to get this job done.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.908
And the kids are absolutely
correct to be furious,

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:06.412
to be frustrated,
to scold us and say,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.982
"Adults, hey, be adults.
Get the job done,"

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.883
and that's what
we're trying to do.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.519
-Obviously,
Paris was reported on in 2015,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.120
when you negotiated
that climate agreement.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.889
Now, we're coming up
and you're preparing

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.891
for Glasgow in the fall.
-Right.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:23.363
-And I believe it's being sold
as our last, best chance.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:26.432
Is that the correct wording?

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.567
-It is the correct wording.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.935
I think I've probably
used those words.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:32.371
Here's where we are.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:36.075
The scientists have made it
clear to us that --

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.376
they made it clear,
three years ago,

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:38.744
that we had 12 years

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.647
within which to make
the most critical decisions,

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:42.882
in order to avoid

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.684
the worst consequences
of the climate crisis.

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:47.987
So, we lost three years
with President Trump.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.022
Now, we're trying
to make up for it

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:51.790
and we're trying to accelerate.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.793
We have nine years,
within which,

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.662
if we don't do enough

00:04:56.662 --> 00:05:00.066
to reduce the emissions
that are already out there,

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:02.935
we can't achieve net zero
by 2050.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.371
If we don't do enough
2020, 2030,

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.573
we can't keep the Earth's
temperature increase

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:11.777
to the 1.5° that the scientists
say we should try to do.

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:13.779
We're at 1.2° now,

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:18.250
so we've got this tiny cushion
of 0.3° of warming

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.654
before things really begin to

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:24.991
snowball out of all proportion.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:29.328
And that's the fear people have.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.531
We have to take advantage
of these 10 years.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:34.333
Right now, I'm proud to say,

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.735
President Biden's
summit produced

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:41.807
55% of the global
enterprise effort, global GDP.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:47.246
Is committed on plans
that will hold the 1.5°.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:50.650
But that means we still have 45%
on the outside of that

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.917
and we've got
to pull them together.

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:54.186
Twenty countries, Seth,

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:58.090
are the equivalent of 80%
of all the emissions.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.092
So we're one of them.
We're number 2.

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:01.259
China's number 1.

00:06:01.259 --> 00:06:03.762
Russia, India, Mexico.

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:05.931
I mean,
a whole group of countries

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:09.468
have got to step up
in the next days, us included,

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:12.104
and we all have to do better
and do more.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:13.773
-And when you talk,
I would imagine,

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.542
when you discuss the countries
you just listed,

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.744
you know, the bigger...

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.646
-...the bigger emitters.
The bigger economies.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.415
-And I would imagine the
approach you have with them all

00:06:23.415 --> 00:06:24.784
has to be very different.

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:26.952
And, you know, based on being
the secretary of state,

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:29.421
the diplomacy involved
must be very delicate.

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:31.023
-Well, every country

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:33.158
brings its own set
of challenges to the table

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:36.595
and every country believes
that it needs

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:39.198
a certain something to be able
to help them get there.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.799
That's what we're busy
doing right now.

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:44.036
We have a great team of people,

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:47.639
experts, many of whom have
negotiated the Paris Agreement

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:50.276
and have been to the other
meetings over the years.

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.144
So, I think we have a good sense

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:54.546
of where we have to go
and how we get there.

00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:58.818
We've got to help some countries
to make the leap

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:01.353
that it's better
on the other side, here.

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:02.921
This is not a choice

00:07:02.921 --> 00:07:04.590
between protecting
the environment

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.526
or having a strong economy.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:10.929
This, they both
can come together.

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:14.666
And what we know is
that the job creation here

00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:16.068
will be just stunning.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.738
I mean, sometimes, you know,

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:21.774
I think about the
United States of America

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.575
invented the Internet.
We went to the Moon.

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:26.579
We have a rover on Mars.

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:28.547
We can remotely send it
around Mars.

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:32.985
We do incredible things,
but we can't send an electron

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:36.189
from California to New York
in the year 2021.

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:38.390
That's crazy, and it's insulting

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.492
because we could have
an energy system

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:44.163
that's more efficient, that's
more effective, that's cheaper.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.498
And we can use AI,
artificial intelligence.

00:07:46.498 --> 00:07:48.534
We can use quantum computing.

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:49.902
We could be ahead of this curve.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:52.037
And we want --
President Biden wants --

00:07:52.037 --> 00:07:54.907
the United States
to lead the effort

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:58.410
to develop the new technologies
to create the capacity

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.580
to make this transition
effectively and on time.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.748
And it's all about kids.

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.583
You have kids.
I have kids, grandkids.

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:06.652
-Yeah.
-This really is

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:08.154
their world we're talking about

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.621
and we need to get
our act together.

00:08:09.621 --> 00:08:11.624
-I'm glad you mentioned kids
because I have one last question

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:14.460
I want to leave you with.
The last time I saw you,

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.994
we were out and I had my son

00:08:15.994 --> 00:08:17.363
and we were both
wearing straw hats

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:18.964
and my son
took off his straw hat

00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:20.900
and I put his straw hat
on top of my straw hat

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.401
and I'd forgotten
that I had done that.

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.670
And then I saw you and I went
over and said hello.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:28.074
Did you know that I was
wearing two straw hats?

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:29.141
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:30.409
-Not only did I know

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:31.844
that you were wearing
two straw hats,

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:34.379
but when I saw that,
when I saw you,

00:08:34.379 --> 00:08:38.618
I said to myself that
George Bush got Will Ferrell

00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:40.552
and I got a guy
who wears two hats.

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:42.421
What the hell is going on here?
-How dare you!

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:44.189
[ Laughter ]
How dare you, sir!

00:08:44.189 --> 00:08:45.558
John Kerry, everybody.

